{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Rubber Pluck Bass",
 "category": "Bass",
 "text": "Sound: a round, rubbery, plucked bass that 'boings' on every note: the bouncy keyboard bass of EBM and synth-pop, played rather than sequenced.\n\nHow it's built: a saw through the OTA filter (its saturating stages give the rubbery tone) with RESONANCE up; a short envelope snaps the filter open and shut; the VCA's envelope decays to a low sustain so held notes stay but the pluck leads. One voice.\n\nPlay: bouncy, staccato bass parts, octave jumps.\n\nTweak: the filter envelope's DECAY (longer is a slower 'boing'), RESONANCE, the filter's CV.",
